Subject: [PATCH 179/213] feat: static BVH per SVO cell for software triangle
 ray tracing (stage 1B)

Replaces the experimental per-voxel triangle list path with one static BVH per
32 m SVO cell, written into a chunk-allocated record pool that the GPU consumer
reads through SVO_RTPoolInfo. Everything is behind e_svoTI_RT_Active; with the
flag off the produced data (bricks, tree texture including texel [1].w and the
.crysvo files) is unchanged.

Pool contract (scene-notes/rt/decisions/02):
- geomPool_Tris is W x W x D R32G32B32A32F, W = e_svoTI_RT_TriPoolXY (256),
  D = e_svoTI_RT_TriPoolZ (64) -> 64 MiB, 1048576 records of 4 texels.
- geomPool_TTex is A x A x Zt RGBA8, A = e_svoTI_RT_MaxTexRes (now 256),
  Zt = e_svoTI_RT_TexPoolZ (256) -> 64 MiB.
- Dimensions have one source of truth in CSvoEnv and reach the renderer through
  the new SSvoStaticTexInfo fields rtPoolXY / rtPoolZ / rtTexRes / rtTexPoolZ.
- The STATIC segment starts at record 49152; record 0 is never a valid root.

Allocator and lifetime:
- First-fit free list over the STATIC segment with 64 record granularity,
  guarded by the record pool's existing lock; materials live at the head of the
  cell's chunk so one free reclaims everything.
- A re-voxelized or deleted cell queues its old chunk and its atlas slice
  references for release; they are applied on the main thread a few frames
  later, so the GPU never sees a freed root.
- Allocation failure gives the cell root 0 (voxel cone tracing fallback) plus a
  once-per-level warning naming the cvar to raise - never silent aliasing.
- The ring buffer write offsets are replaced by a dirty Z slice bitset; only
  dirty slices are uploaded.

Builder (decision 03): binned SAH, 3 axes x 16 bins on the centroid bounds,
Ct = Ci = 1, exact child bounds, median fallback, leaf <= e_svoTI_RT_LeafTris,
depth <= e_svoTI_RT_MaxDepth, deterministic, terrain included, visarea seal
shells excluded. The build runs on the streaming worker into a local buffer and
takes the pool lock only to reserve the chunk and memcpy the finished records,
so e_svoTI_NumStreamingThreads is no longer forced to 1 and the decompression
job is no longer disabled when RT is active.

Records are byte exact per decision 02 section 2.5; the CPU packers are the
exact inverses of the shader helpers (PackU16x2/ExtractPosXY, PackDir/ExtractDir,
PackTC16/ExtractTC16, PackUint2/ExtractUint2). Per-cell quantisation bounds are
written into every node so shared vertices quantise identically.

Material atlas (decision 04): albedo (EFTT_DIFFUSE) and normal (_ddna,
EFTT_NORMALS) layers via GetLowResSystemCopy, free list over Z slices with
refcounts, terrain slot as before. BC5 normals arrive with only two valid
channels from DXTDecompressRow, so the blue channel is reconstructed on copy.

Retired with the per-voxel path: StoreAreaTrisIntoTriPool, StoreIndicesIntoPool,
m_arrRTPoolInds, m_texTrisPoolId and the RTRIS brick sub-set writes.
GetSubSetsNum() now stays 3 with RT on, so exported .crysvo files keep their
meaning. e_svoTI_RT_SafetyBorder and e_svoTI_RT_MaxTrisPerVoxel stay registered
but are marked deprecated so existing level files keep loading.

e_svoTI_RT_SelfTest 1 builds a synthetic soup (two quads plus a thin wall),
writes real records and then CPU-traces 1000 rays through those records with a
reference traversal that mirrors decision 02, comparing against brute force.

